   "Breadboard placement is my own choice. Each wire goes to a top-half column (a), the resistor spans the centre gap (row b top to row f bottom), the LED anode sits in the same bottom strip (row g), and the LED cathode goes into the bottom negative rail 'bn', which wire7 connects to Uno GND.1.",
   "Pins 2-7 are wired in order to led1-led6. The sketch's array order {2,7,4,6,5,3} only affects the lighting sequence, not the wiring."
  ]
 },
